From 51e3d0768b5b60dabf45c829a28e4fee53d1f97f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Maestro <jjmaestro@ieee.org>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 06:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch: widen the gap between the two settings snapshots

The suite asserts twice that the recorded reboot is in the past by more than a
fixed interval:

    SELECT now() - ts > interval '2 second' FROM "PGTS".pg_reboot;
    SELECT now() - ts > interval '2 second' FROM "PGTS".pg_track_reboot_log();

`ts` is the postmaster start time, so both hold only if the server has been up
for over two seconds by the time the test reaches them. Run against a
long-lived instance that is never in question. Run under a pg_regress
`--temp-instance`, the server is started moments before the suite, and the only
thing between startup and those two queries is the suite itself, which takes
well under two seconds. Both then return `f` and the test fails, on a timing
detail rather than on anything the extension did.

Widening the settings-history `pg_sleep` from 1 to 3 seconds puts the elapsed
time above the threshold before the reboot section is reached. That sleep is
there to separate two configuration snapshots in time, and everything asserted
about it only needs the gap to be large enough: the log still shows the same
two `work_mem` rows, and `pg_track_settings_diff(now() - interval '500 ms',
now())` still sees only the second change.
---
 expected/pg_track_settings.out | 2 +-
 test/sql/pg_track_settings.sql | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/expected/pg_track_settings.out b/expected/pg_track_settings.out
index 8fea4e6..2c11b6d 100644
--- a/expected/pg_track_settings.out
+++ b/expected/pg_track_settings.out
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ SELECT * FROM "PGTS".pg_track_settings_snapshot();
  t
 (1 row)
 
-SELECT pg_catalog.pg_sleep(1);
+SELECT pg_catalog.pg_sleep(3);
  pg_sleep 
 ----------
  
diff --git a/test/sql/pg_track_settings.sql b/test/sql/pg_track_settings.sql
index aef6131..b43a19f 100644
--- a/test/sql/pg_track_settings.sql
+++ b/test/sql/pg_track_settings.sql
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@ ORDER BY descr COLLATE "C";
 SELECT COUNT(*) FROM "PGTS".pg_track_settings_history;
 SET work_mem = '10MB';
 SELECT * FROM "PGTS".pg_track_settings_snapshot();
-SELECT pg_catalog.pg_sleep(1);
+SELECT pg_catalog.pg_sleep(3);
 SET work_mem = '5MB';
 SELECT * FROM "PGTS".pg_track_settings_snapshot();
 SELECT name, setting_exists, setting, setting_pretty FROM "PGTS".pg_track_settings_log('work_mem') ORDER BY ts ASC;
